From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MI50 ROCm 10.x project <mi50-rocm10@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rocBLAS: keep gfx906 on the Tensile backend by default

hipBLASLt is compiled as a forward-port candidate for gfx906, but its
TensileLite kernel coverage is not yet a supported MI50 path. Use the mature
rocBLAS/Tensile backend by default and preserve ROCBLAS_USE_HIPBLASLT=1 as an
explicit opt-in for hardware experiments.

---
 projects/rocblas/library/src/tensile_host.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/projects/rocblas/library/src/tensile_host.cpp b/projects/rocblas/library/src/tensile_host.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/projects/rocblas/library/src/tensile_host.cpp
+++ b/projects/rocblas/library/src/tensile_host.cpp
@@ -1140,3 +1140,12 @@ bool useHipBLASLt(const RocblasContractionProblem<Ti, To, Tc>& prob)
 {
 #ifdef BUILD_WITH_HIPBLASLT
+    // MI50/gfx906 uses rocBLAS/Tensile unless hipBLASLt is explicitly forced.
+    // This keeps a provisional backend from becoming an accidental runtime
+    // dependency while retaining a controlled opt-in for later validation.
+    if(rocblas_internal_get_arch(prob.handle) == 906
+       && !prob.handle->isHipBLASLtForcedOn())
+    {
+        return false;
+    }
+
     if constexpr(sizeof(Ti) >= 4)
--
2.45.2
